# SMMOL — what stays out of the repo.
#
# Three rules:
#   1. Nothing personal. The harness is software Andrew actually uses; its run logs and
#      conversations are real usage, not test data.
#   2. No weights or corpora. Two checkpoints exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit and git-lfs
#      is not in play. Every README says how to retrain from scratch.
#   3. Nothing a rerun regenerates.

# ---- Trained weights ----------------------------------------------------------------
# ~1.2 GB across the projects. Retrain with each project's documented command.
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.gguf
*.bin

# ---- Corpora and derived splits -----------------------------------------------------
# Targeted by name, not by a blanket data/raw/ rule: archive/models/smSOFTWARE_ENGINEERING_001/data/raw/
# holds a provenance manifest with pinned commits and upstream license files, which is
# exactly the kind of thing a public repo should carry. Fetch scripts stay tracked too.
#
# TinyStories is not ours to redistribute; Tiny Shakespeare is small but still a download.
models/smLANGUAGE_EN_001/data/raw/
models/smLANGUAGE_EN_001/data/train.txt
models/smLANGUAGE_EN_001/data/val.txt
models/smLANGUAGE_EN_001/data/test.txt
models/smLLM_01/data/input.txt

# 483 KB of verbatim source from 75 other people's repositories. Permissively licensed
# (MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD-3-Clause) and properly attributed, so redistributing it would be
# legal — but smSOFTWARE_ENGINEERING_001/README.md says "review the manifest and original
# repositories before publishing a corpus or weights", and not shipping someone else's
# code under our own repo's licence is the cleaner call. github_corpus.py rebuilds it
# byte-for-byte from the pinned commits and blob SHAs in the manifest, which IS tracked,
# along with every upstream licence text.
archive/models/smSOFTWARE_ENGINEERING_001/data/raw/records.jsonl

# ---- Live harness state -------------------------------------------------------------
# Real conversations, real memory, real run transcripts. Every one is read through
# `read_json(path, default)`, and `module_on()` falls back to each module's own `enabled`
# flag in harness.json — which IS tracked. So a fresh clone starts with the intended
# defaults and writes its own state on first run. Nothing here needs a committed example.
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/conversations/
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/memory/
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/runs/
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/scores.json
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/settings.json
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/switches.json
harnesses/paratroop_harness_*/choices.json

# ---- Training output ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Results and logs ARE the experimental record and are deliberately tracked — the research
# log cites them. Only scratch and intermediate artifacts are ignored.
**/out/**/tmp/
**/out/**/scratch/
**/checkpoints/**/optimizer.pt

# ---- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- Agent scratch ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code puts agent worktrees under .claude/worktrees/, inside the repo. Each is a
# full checkout, so a stray `git add -A` would otherwise stage tens of MB of duplicate
# tree. Scoped to the volatile subdirs so a future .claude/skills/ can still be committed
# on purpose.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/tasks/

# ---- Editors and OS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.obsidian/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# ---- Local secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here today. The line exists so it stays that way.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.netrc
